./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-02-transcription-settings-design.md:8:Memos has one AI feature today: audio transcription (speech-to-text). The current design has three concrete problems:
./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-02-transcription-settings-design.md:11:2. **No explicit transcription configuration.** `InstanceAISetting.providers` is a generic credentials list. The frontend (`MemoEditor/index.tsx:65`) implicitly picks "the first provider with an API key whose type is in TRANSCRIPTION_PROVIDER_TYPES." Users cannot:
./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-02-transcription-settings-design.md:25:- Per-call provider override at recording time. Research across all surveyed products (OpenWebUI, LibreChat, Whisper Memos, Superwhisper, etc.) confirms STT engine is a global preference, not an action-time choice. We follow the same pattern.
./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-02-transcription-settings-design.md:27:- Multi-user or per-user override of admin defaults. Memos' STT setting is instance-scoped, like every other instance setting.
./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-02-transcription-settings-design.md:31:Field and message names follow cross-platform STT conventions, not Memos-internal shorthand:
./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-02-transcription-settings-design.md:35:| Config message | `TranscriptionConfig` | AssemblyAI uses this exact identifier; matches OpenAI's `CreateTranscription*` verb family and Memos' existing `Transcribe` RPC. The `STT` acronym is not used as a type name in any major STT API. |
./docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-02-transcription-settings-design.md:41:A note on the message name collision: `proto/api/v1/ai_service.proto` already declares a `TranscriptionConfig` for **per-call** prompt/language overrides. The new store-level `TranscriptionConfig` lives in package `memos.store`, so the two compile cleanly. Memos already uses parallel `api.v1.X` / `store.X` message pairs (e.g. `User`, `Memo`); this matches that pattern.
